{"uid":"cc1182a16603ff63","name":"test_the_shared_context_refuses_obsolete_protocols","fullName":"tests.framework.test_tls#test_the_shared_context_refuses_obsolete_protocols","time":{"start":1794913177620,"stop":1794913177620,"duration":0},"description":"TLS 1.0 and 1.1 must never be explicitly re-enabled here.\n\n    This assertion used to be ``minimum_version >= TLSv1_2`` and it failed the\n    moment the suite ran in a container:\n\n        assert <TLSVersion.MINIMUM_SUPPORTED: -2> >= <TLSVersion.TLSv1_2: 771>\n\n    Both environments are secure. ``MINIMUM_SUPPORTED`` means \"whatever this\n    OpenSSL build's system policy allows\", which on Ubuntu 24.04 is TLS 1.2 -\n    the platform simply expresses the same guarantee with a different value.\n\n    So the original test was asserting a **platform default**, not a property of\n    this framework, and it would keep breaking on every OS whose OpenSSL is\n    configured differently. What this module actually controls is that it does\n    not *weaken* anything, and that is what is asserted now: the two obsolete\n    versions are never explicitly selected.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>TLS 1.0 and 1.1 must never be explicitly re-enabled here.</p>\n<pre><code>This assertion used to be ``minimum_version &gt;= TLSv1_2`` and it failed the\nmoment the suite ran in a container:\n\n    assert &lt;TLSVersion.MINIMUM_SUPPORTED: -2&gt; &gt;= &lt;TLSVersion.TLSv1_2: 771&gt;\n\nBoth environments are secure. ``MINIMUM_SUPPORTED`` means &quot;whatever this\nOpenSSL build's system policy allows&quot;, which on Ubuntu 24.04 is TLS 1.2 -\nthe platform simply expresses the same guarantee with a different value.\n\nSo the original test was asserting a **platform default**, not a property of\nthis framework, and it would keep breaking on every OS whose OpenSSL is\nconfigured differently. What this module actually controls is that it does\nnot *weaken* anything, and that is what is asserted now: the two obsolete\nversions are never explicitly selected.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1794913165994,"stop":1794913166060,"duration":66},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"delete_output_dir","time":{"start":1794913166060,"stop":1794913166060,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"settings","time":{"start":1794913166060,"stop":1794913166061,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"pytestconfig","time":{"start":1794913166060,"stop":1794913166060,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"artifacts","time":{"start":1794913166061,"stop":1794913166061,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_framework_logging","time":{"start":1794913166062,"stop":1794913166062,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1794913168577,"stop":1794913168577,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},{"n